<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    An ELF function name that shares its address with an earlier symbol still
    selects that function (loader-tier fix, no option).

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture. The script clears it
    and loads a real ARM32 shared object built from committed assembly
    (`armveneeralias_le32.s`, clang + ld.lld): the exported `answer` sits at the
    same address as the local ARM veneer name `__answer_from_arm`, which comes
    first in `.symtab`, and a Thumb `caller` reaches `answer` through the PLT, so
    `answer` also labels the PLT stub.

    The loader used to keep one name per address, so `answer` survived only on
    the PLT stub and `load function answer` decompiled the stub:
    `(*dat_30274)(); // jump-as-call`. The dropped names are now kept as aliases
    of the entry, and the definition wins over its import stub, so both names
    reach the veneer's body. The reported name at that address, and the name
    call sites print, stay `__answer_from_arm` / `answer` as before.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/armveneeralias_le32</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function answer</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function __answer_from_arm</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function caller</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="ELFALIASNAMES #1: the exported name no longer selects the PLT stub" min="0" max="0">jump-as-call</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ELFALIASNAMES #2: the exported name decompiles the definition" min="1" max="1">unsigned int answer\(void\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ELFALIASNAMES #3: both names reach the same body" min="2" max="2">return 7;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="ELFALIASNAMES #4: the call through the PLT keeps its name" min="1" max="1">  answer\(\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
